    2. Choose even grid dimensions H, W each in [4, 12]
    3. Partition into (H/2) x (W/2) blocks; assign rotation k to block (br, bc) via rot = (br + bc) % 4 (guarantees top-left = rot0 and uses all 4 rotations for grids >= 4x4)
    4. Fill each block with np.rot90(seed, k) to produce the input grid
